Author_Conclusion:
CONCLUSIONS This field study revealed a relationship between higher cardiorespiratory fitness and lower mean HR and peak BCT values throughout the long distance march. During the breaks, no evidence indicated a different recovery behavior for HR or BCT between the three groups. The rapid recovery of the energy stores should be given the utmost attention, as the entire sample showed an enormous energy deficit regardless of fitness level. A higher \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
